condition_name: Pericoronitis
condition_slug: pericoronitis
source: NSTG 2022
introduction: An inflammatory condition of the operculum or gum flap around a partially erupted/impacted tooth. Common around the lower last molars or wisdom teeth.
clinical_features[1]:
  - type: General
    features[6]: Soreness and tenderness around partially-erupted tooth,Pain,Swelling,Enlargement of regional lymph nodes,Fever,Abscess formation
investigations[3]: Radiographs,To establish the position of the affected tooth and its relationship to the second molar,May show impacted third molar
treatment:
  goals[0]:
  non_drug[5]: "Careful irrigation under the gum flap to clear debris, using warm saline mouthwash; To be done frequently until stagnation area is removed",Operculectomy,Disimpaction of the third molar by surgical extraction,Occlusal reduction of opposing tooth,Extraction of opposing tooth to forestall supraeruption and sequelae
  drug[3]: Appropriate antibiotics,Analgesics,Supportive therapy
  adverse_reactions_and_cautions[0]:
  supportive_measures[0]:
differential_diagnoses[0]:
complications[5]: Cellulitis,Ludwig's angina,Osteomyelitis,Submasseteric abscess,Temporomandibular joint ankylosis
prevention[0]:
other_investigations: null
definitive_treatment: null
prognosis: null